#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Reproduce-on-Read (step 2.4): this hook no longer writes to the ledger.
#
# It used to run `truth invalidate-scan`, which asks a SYNTACTIC question --
# did git touch a watched path -- and appends an `invalidation` record for
# every yes. Measured on this ledger: 1971 such records against 70 actual
# evidence divergences. Positive predictive value 3.6%; at least 65% were
# provably empty (the mechanical `reaffirm` arm re-ran the recipe and got a
# byte-identical result). The absorbing machinery that made that bearable --
# reaffirm plus the `reaffirm_cleared` field -- had itself grown to 28% of
# the ledger, read by nothing.
#
# The direct measurement costs ~8ms per capsule (0.53s for the whole live
# ledger), so the proxy was an optimisation for an operation that is free at
# this scale. `truth reproduce` is now the authority and runs as an arm of
# the release battery at pre-push, where it blocks on exit 7 and on exit 8.
#
# Nothing replaces the write here on purpose: a green sweep should leave no
# record, because there is no stored state left to advance.
exit 0
